   "notes": "Described the pretrained Llama 2 base model. The 7B config is primary. The 7B/13B widths, depths and head counts are given as inherited from Llama 1, based on the paper's explicit sentence 'We adopt most of the pretraining setting and model architecture from Llama 1'. Its stated differences are only the context length (4096) and GQA. 34B and 70B are new sizes with no Llama 1 counterpart, so their sizes are not_stated except kv_heads=8. That value comes from the GQA variant 'with 8 KV projections', which the paper chose for 34B/70B. d_ff is not stated anywhere (only ablation FFN multipliers 1.3/1.33 are given). Norm eps, RoPE pairing/theta, biases and tied embeddings are not stated; the eps=1e-5 in the paper is AdamW's. The final RMSNorm in the head is not stated in the text. The reward model (same architecture with a regression head) and Ghost Attention (a data/fine-tuning technique) are not architectural changes to the network."
  },
